CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionARC	<ul>\n<li><strong>Account Contact Relationship</strong> object: defines the relationship between a person and a business or other account.</li>\n<li><strong>Account – Account Relationship</strong> object: defines the relationship between businesses, institutions, and groups.</li>\n<li><strong>Contact - Contact Relationship</strong> object: defines the relationship between two people.</li>\n<li><strong>Reciprocal Role</strong>: Stores roles that define the patterns of social interaction between related statuses. eg. Husband & Wife or Grandparent & Grandchild</li>\n</ul>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionB2BExpandedAccountRel	<strong>Pro tip</strong>: Expanded Account relationship allows easy to view a parent company and its subsidiaries, when business record types are defined as Groups, in the enhanced Relationship Map.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionBestPractices	The following section provides a high level summary of best practices related to the impacted components based on the objects selected for mapping. Always consider the end state needs while selecting appropriate approaches for data models.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionBusinessTransformationOpportunity	A business transformation assessment is a comprehensive review and audit of how users are using the current functionality in Salesforce. Here you should focus on the key capabilities and see if the current implementation is delivering the desired business value. If the current functionality is not delivering the desired business value, identify how to improve the current solution to meet the business needs.\n<br/><br/>\nMoving to a customer-centric view is another reason why business transformation may be needed. If the current implementation uses Product centric view and business processes built around that, it is highly recommended to start with a new org as FSC uses customer-centric view. Keep in mind, some of the business process may be impacted as you move from product centric to customer-centric view. Additionally, assess the impact of either new features that need to be rolled out to existing users or new users that needs to be on-boarded.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionChangeManagement	The last area of assessment is change management. Consider how each approach is going to impact the end user and how you can reduce the end user impact. If you decide to upgrade an existing org, rolling out FSC functionality in multiple releases may be a better approach.\n<br/><br/>\nWhile this report focuses on Technology aspects of the FSC transition, the importance of business uplift or impact cannot be minimized. You should assess business uplift opportunities that can have some impact on the approach.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionComponentsCovered	This report does not cover the impact in following areas based on the fields and objects that were mapped.\n<br/><br/>\n<ul>\n<li>Private Reports/Dashboards</li>\n<li>Private List Views</li>\n<li>Duplicate Rules</li>\n</ul>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionExpandedARs	<a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_create_expanded_aar.htm">Enable expanded Account Relationships</a> in Group Builder to support directly associating businesses and legal entities, such as trusts, to households and groups.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionFSCIcon	To enhance the user experience and to quickly gain insight into a customer's Life Events & Business Milestones it is possible to define an icon per Life Event/Business Milestone. For more information, visit this link: <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_custom_icons_for_event_milestone_types.htm">https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_custom_icons_for_event_milestone_types.htm</a>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionFSCRollups	FSC supports rolling up individual client related information related to the client's primary household. Refer to additional information related to <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_record_rollups.htm">Record Rollups</a>. If you chose not to use rollups in FSC, you can disable “Enable Group Record Rollups” and/or “Enable Rollup Summary” through <strong><em>Wealth Application Config</em></strong> <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_custom_settings.htm?search_text=wealth">custom settings</a>.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionFinancialAccountRole	Additionally, if your business needs to support more than two owners on a Financial Account, leverage Financial Account Role (FAR) to capture the owners. Leverage Financial Account Role List component in the client 360 view to include all Financial Account where this client has some kind of ownership.\n<br/><br/>\nFollow best practices while loading data into FA and FAR object. For large volumes of data load, sort the Financial Account input file on Primary Owner as system locks corresponding Account record while loading or updating Financial Account. In addition, if the FA system of record does not have a primary owner, ensure there is a consistent way of identifying the primary owner. If owner information is switched during data load, you may end up creating too many records in FAR object.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionFinancialAccounts	Primary owner on Financial Account (FA) is required information in FSC. If your data set has some Financial Accounts with no Primary owner, consider bringing them later in the transformation. This will give you some time to identify Primary owners for such Financial Accounts. If you have to create a fictitious primary owner, ensure that you are not creating a data skew on the Primary owner. Refer to <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/engineering/2013/04/managing-lookup-skew-to-avoid-record-lock-exceptions.html">Managing Lookup Skew in Salesforce to Avoid Record Lock Exceptions</a> for best practices.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionFinancialBalance	We highly recommend loading end of day balance information in FSC. This will help you in leveraging FSC Rollup functionalities to build Household 360 view. As a best practice, use the <a href="https://help.salesforce.com/articleView?id=sf.concept_data_processing_engine.htm&type=5">Data Process Engine</a> to rollup Financial Account balances.\n<br/><br/>\nFor large data volume scenarios (>5M records), understand when the updates will be available and the frequency of updates (daily vs weekly). Use small batch size while updating the Financial Account object. Account update processes and Financial Account updates may need to be streamlined to reduce locking issues.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionHouseholdGroup	Follow the <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_config_group_custom_record.htm">instructions</a> to ensure all Household / Group record types are updated in <strong><em>Group Record Type Mapper</em></strong> custom metadata. It is recommended to use Actionable Relationship Center (ARC) for HH / Group 360 view. ARC leverages the following data model to store and manage the relationship information.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionISVConsiderations	The other key consideration is the number of ISV solutions you have in the current org and how complex it is to move or re-implement them to a new org. Some of these ISV solutions are complex and reimplementing may take a good amount of effort. In addition, check with your ISV provider if there is prebuilt integration with FSC. Some of the ISV solutions are complex and may need considerable effort in case of new org implementation.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionInsurance	Data model objects can be associated with each other in numerous ways. What’s important to keep in mind is that not all associations are required for all scenarios. It depends on the scale of business, the operations you want to perform, and the kind of products or services you’re targeting.\n<br/><br/>\nLorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Bibendum neque egestas congue quisque egestas diam in arcu cursus. Vestibulum rhoncus est pellentesque elit ullamcorper. Vel facilisis volutpat est velit egestas dui. Ultrices in iaculis nunc sed augue lacus viverra vitae congue. Accumsan sit amet nulla facilisi morbi tempus. Viverra mauris in aliquam sem fringilla ut morbi tincidunt augue. Bibendum enim facilisis gravida neque convallis a. Nibh tortor id aliquet lectus proin nibh nisl.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionInsuranceIcon	For an enhanced user experience, it is possible to define icons per insurance type so that the type can be recognized quickly and easily. For more information, visit this link: <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_insurance_admin_use_slds_icons.htm">https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_insurance_admin_use_slds_icons.htm</a>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionInsuranceSpecificFeatures	Financial Services Cloud provides options to tailor Insurance functionality to your specific needs. Please refer to the <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_insurance_admin_setup.htm">Set Up Insurance for Financial Services Cloud</a> section in the Admin Guide for Financial Services Cloud.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionModelBusinessAndIndividual	FSC uses Person Accounts to model individual clients and Contacts to model business contacts. It is generally a best practice to use two records, one Person Account for the B2C relationship and Contacts for B2B relationship when the same individual happens to be a Retail client as well as small business / commercial banking contact. If you have to use a single record to model both relationships, use a personal account record type. Here are some considerations when you should manage two records:\n<br/><br/>\n<ul>\n<li>If you are planning to use Partner community in future, Account + Contact model will be best to model Business contacts</li>\n<li>If you want keep retail banker / advisor interactions separate from commercial banker interactions, use two different records</li>\n</ul>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionModelBusinessContacts	FSC uses Contact objects to model business contacts.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionModelIndividualClients	FSC uses Person Accounts to model individual clients. Define different person account record types to represent different sets of clients. Once all person account record types are created, update <strong><em>Individual RecordType Mapper</em></strong> <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_config_indiv_custom_record.htm">custom metadata</a> to ensure FSC Individual related functionality works properly.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionNewOrg	Depending on the status of your current implementation, you may have to upgrade your current org or you may have to start with a new org . There are certain advantages with each of these approaches. It is critical to analyze the three areas discussed above and make an informed decision on which approach is the best approach for your situation.\n<br/><br/>\nHere are a few important factors that other customers have used to decide whether to start with new org or upgrade existing org. In general, these customers had more than one reason why they chose one approach over the other.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionNewOrgTable1	<table class="slds-table slds-table_cell-buffer slds-table_bordered slds-table_col-bordered slds-table_header-hidden slds-no-row-hover slds-table_striped">\n<thead>\n<th></th>\n<th>Start New Financial Services Cloud Org</th>\n<th>Upgrade Existing Org to Financial Services Cloud</th>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Business Transformation</td>\n<td class="slds-cell-wrap">Redesign existing business capabilities to deliver higher business impact using customer-centric view</td>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionNewOrgTable2	<td class="slds-cell-wrap">Enhance existing customer-centric view with Financial Services Cloud capabilities</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Technology Rationalization</td>\n<td>More customization to redesign<br>Need to reimplement ISV integrations</td>\n<td>Limited customization<br>Refactor existing ISV integrations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change Management</td>\n<td>Train users on larger changes in one release</td>\n<td>Train users on smaller changes over multiple releases</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionNextSteps1	<ol><li>Assess potential redesign opportunities and pain points with the current solution. FSC transition is a good opportunity to address some of these pain points and align with the FSC data model.</li>\n<li>Decide on whether to start with new org or upgrade existing org. Each approach presents different levels of opportunities in different areas. Also, both approaches have their own pros and cons, so decide on the approach before starting a development effort. Always keep the target state in mind while deciding on the approach.</li>\n<li>Complete the data architecture / data model mapping before loading the data</li>\n<li>Evaluate <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_common_capabilities.htm?search_text=wealth">Common Capabilities in FSC</a> and identify additional capabilities that can help the business</li>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionNextSteps2	<li>Build an implementation roadmap. If there is a large amount of data to transform, implement data model changes prior to the release. This will provide additional time to transform the data.</li>\n<li>If you are starting with a new org, consider creating custom objects to store the field history. Also, plan ahead to extract and load the historical and all related data from old salesforce org to new org.</li>\n<li>Generated deployment package includes profiles and permission sets updated with FSC objects and fields. Permissions for old custom objects need to be manually updated to either remove access or change it to read only.</li>\n<li>Once data from mapped custom objects is transformed to FSC objects, consider archiving the data from salesforce org</li><ol>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionPersonAccountPrimaryContact	While using person account, <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.226.0.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_disable_primary_contact_id.htm">disable updates to Primary Contact Field</a> on Account to reduce additional overhead.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionPersonAccounts1	Use single Person Account record when:\n<br><br>\n<ul>\n<li>Consolidated 360 view is needed with all interactions</li>\n<li>Customer is never going to implement Partner Portal</li>\n<li>Need to avoid Person Account conversions during data sync from MDM/system of record</li>\n</ul>\n<br>\nKeep in mind Salesforce supports converting a <a href="https://help.salesforce.com/articleView?id=sf.leads_notes.htm&type=5">Lead into PersonAccount and a Business Account</a>.\n<br>
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionPersonAccounts2	Define different person account record types to represent different sets of clients. Once all person account record types are created, update <strong><em>Individual RecordType Mapper</em></strong> <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.financial_services_cloud_admin_guide.meta/financial_services_cloud_admin_guide/fsc_admin_config_indiv_custom_record.htm">custom metadata</a> to ensure FSC Individual related functionality works properly. If you have to convert Contacts into Person Account records, we recommend engaging an expert to guide you through the process.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionPlanningYourTransition	You can transition to FSC either by starting with a new org or installing FSC in the current org. Vast majority of our FSC customers who transitioned from Sales or Service Cloud have made their decision, whether to implement FSC in the current org or implement FSC in the new org, based on their analysis in three major areas.
CustomLabel.FSCTransition__AssessmentReportSubsectionTechnologyRationalization	The second area of assessment is around technology. In addition to reviewing the findings in the following section, consider the amount of data you have in the current implementation and effort to migrate to a new org. Will there be a need to keep the data in-sync between new and old org for a short duration if you decide to implement it in a new org. Will the backend integrations work if you have to integrate with two instances at the same time. If you have considerable data transformation effort, consider implementing object model changes a few days before the release. This will provide additional time to finish the data updates.\n<br/><br/>\nIn addition to data volume, evaluate the amount of customization that can be retired by replacing current capabilities with FSC features. Starting with a new org will be best if there are a lot of customizations that need to be retired.
